{"name":"Light Tip Toes","hex":"#e1d0d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"tip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Trimuris."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The extreme end of something, especially when pointed; e.g. the sharp end of a pencil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A piece of metal, fabric or other material used to cover the top of something for protection, utility or decoration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tip"},{"term":"toes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of toe"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of toe"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tip Toes","blocks":[{"text":"Tip Toes is a 1927 British silent film comedy-drama, directed by Herbert Wilcox and starring Dorothy Gish and Will Rogers. The film is a loose adaptation of the stage musical Tip-Toes, with the action transferred from Florida to London."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/%22Tip_Toes%22_%281927_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tip_Toes","wikidata":"Q7808776"},{"title":"Toe","blocks":[{"text":"Toes are the digits of the foot of a tetrapod. Animal species such as cats that walk on their toes are described as being digitigrade. Humans, and other animals that walk on the soles of their feet, are described as being plantigrade; unguligrade animals are those that walk on hooves at the tips of their toes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Toes.png/330px-Toes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toe","wikidata":"Q154425"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Gray269.png/500px-Gray269.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Gray269.png/500px-Gray269.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bones of the right foot. Plantar surface.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray269.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm